>> title: Gỏi Cuốn
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: pork, shrimp, vietnamese, no cook, rice paper
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: goi cuon, gỏi cuốn, fresh spring rolls, spring rolls, summer rolls, salad rolls, rice paper rolls, cold rolls, A2
>> pairs-with: nuoc-cham
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: poach 12 min, cool and slice
>> step.2: boil 4 min, rinse cold
>> step.3: soften, fill and roll tight
>> step.4: stir the peanut sauce
>> step.5: arrange whole or halved, with the sauce

Poach @pork belly{8%oz}(225 g; in one piece) and @shrimp{16%large}(450 g; shell on) in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) with @kosher salt{1%tsp} ~poach{12%min}, lifting the shrimp out after three minutes and the pork at twelve, then cool both, slice the pork thin and split each shrimp lengthways.

Boil @rice vermicelli{4%oz}(115 g) in @hot water{2%qt}(1.9 L) ~boil{4%min}, then drain and rinse cold so the strands stop sticking to each other.

Soften @rice paper wrappers{12} one at a time in @warm water{1%qt}(950 mL), lay @&(~1)noodles{} and @&(~2)pork and shrimp{} across the near third with @lettuce{12%leaves}, @mint{1/2%cup} and @garlic chives{12}(left whole, sticking out one end), then roll tight, tucking the sides in on the second turn. The shrimp go cut side down against the wrapper so they show pink through it.

Stir @hoisin sauce{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @peanut butter{2%Tbs}(30 g), @warm water{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @roasted peanuts{2%Tbs}(chopped) into a dipping sauce loose enough to fall off a spoon.

Arrange @&(~2)rolls{} whole, or halved on a sharp diagonal, alongside @&(~1)peanut sauce{}. Nước chấm is the other correct answer, and half the tables in the room will ask for both.
